    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `frai` CLI was using commander.js to parse arguments, but when delegating to the `frai-gate` subprocess, it only forwarded the positional arguments (`args` parameter), not the flags. This meant the `--ci` flag was lost during the delegation.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-757) to:\n1. Access the raw `process.argv` to find all original arguments\n2. Locate the `'gate'` command in `process.argv`\n3. Pass all arguments after `'gate'` to the spawned `frai-gate` process, preserving all flags\n\n**Verification:**\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested with `node frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` from a clean directory\n- Confirmed both files are now created:\n  - \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n  - \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe fix ensures all command-line arguments (positional and flags) are correctly passed through to the `frai-gate` subprocess.",
